# Project Artifacts
Artifacts/

# Feedback submissions (real user emails/messages, not for version control)
# Runtime state the backend writes to its own tree (feedback log, and
# anything else that follows it). Source root stays source.
backend/data/

# Forecasting engine artifacts (backend/forecasting/, backend/models/).
#
# `backend/models/forecasting/` used to be ignored here on the reasoning that
# the models are reproducible from config, so they should be built rather than
# committed. They are now tracked through Git LFS instead — see .gitattributes.
# Reproducible is not the same as cheap: a full retrain is hours of Copernicus
# fetching, and a single forecast grid is ~35 min of it, so "rebuild it" is a
# real cost to impose on a fresh clone. The rejected horizons are kept for the
# same reason CLAUDE.md gives for not deleting them — the artifact is the
# evidence for the shipping-bar decision.
#
# The fetch cache below stays ignored: it is a local disk cache keyed on a
# fetch window, not an artifact anyone would want back.
backend/forecasting/.cache/

# Experiment tracking store (machine_learning/marine_ml/tracking.py).
# Local run history — SQLite plus per-run artifacts. Machine-specific and it
# grows without bound, so it is not version controlled. Nothing here is a
# source of truth: every run is reproducible, and the backend's runs can be
# rebuilt at any time with `python -m marine_ml.ingest_forecasting`.
machine_learning/mlruns.db
machine_learning/mlruns/

# Claude Code worktrees — full checkouts of this repo (~1 GB), created and
# removed by the agent harness. Never version-controlled inside itself.
.claude/worktrees/
